108:## T9 — Usage accounting, processing tickets, and idempotency
110:Task: Server-only usage records per company per day (America/Sao_Paulo) with atomic reservation against the limit; 
signed processing tickets (issue time, user, company, note, source revision, transcript identity, settings revision; 
HMAC with a server-only secret; valid 24 h); idempotency keys scoped to user+company+operation and bound to that 
payload; operation records without content kept 30 days (pg_cron cleanup); an operation without outcome 10 minutes 
after dispatch becomes "failed" and stays counted (pg_cron); settlement once, against the admission day, only by 
server code; deleting notes or users never changes usage; no client role can read-modify usage beyond its own 
company's count.
112:Verify by: Integration tests for AC-028 (19/20 with five concurrent starts; replay same key/binding across 
midnight; changed binding rejected; direct client refund attempts denied), AC-034 (discarded replay status; expired 
ticket after record cleanup; crash → failed after 10 min, counted; note deletion leaves usage), AC-016 (limit reached 
message data, midnight reset); `supabase-rls-reviewer` audit.
128:Task: Server-only adapters: Anthropic via `@anthropic-ai/sdk`, OpenAI via `openai`, Kimi and GLM via the OpenAI 
SDK with their OpenAI-compatible base URLs; SDK retries disabled (`maxRetries: 0`); each sends only the matrix's valid 
parameters for the chosen model and reasoning level; output requested and validated against one draft schema (summary 
sections, ≤100 items with description and assignee name as written); malformed/truncated output is a failure; an 
input-size preflight against the model's context/output budget refuses oversize transcripts before dispatch; provider 
errors are mapped to sanitized messages and classified as pre-processing rejection only per the matrix. A local fake 
AI server (test-only, started by the integration setup and the E2E runner, selected by a server-only base-URL override 
that is refused when `NODE_ENV=production`) speaks each provider's API, records received requests, and scripts 
outcomes (success, error after processing, timeout, refusal, malformed JSON, listed rejections, unlisted statuses, 
overload mid-stream, connection drop after acceptance, pause/resume).
137:Task: A start route requires a valid ticket bound to the current settings revision (stale → refused with the new 
provider name), reserves usage, snapshots provider/key/model/effort, dispatches once via T11, resolves suggested names 
locally (exact full name, else unique first name, case/accent-insensitive, current members only), rechecks membership 
and note existence before returning, honors client abort with best-effort outbound abort, and settles usage. An Apply 
RPC accepts the edited summary and accepted items only at the draft's source revision, rechecks rights in the 
transaction, marks suggestions duplicating existing items, appends accepted items under T2's shared capacity rule, 
writes the summary, and creates one version — or changes nothing.
