# PLAN: phase-6-meeting-notes

Spec: ./SPEC.md
Goal: Company members can record, revise, search, and export meeting notes per space — with action items, version 
history, and an AI-generated draft summary and action items from an uploaded transcript using the company's own AI 
provider key.
Plan version: 1
Highest task ID reserved: T15

## Standing rules for every task

- **Migration rule (SPEC §9, §10):** a migration is done when it is written, applied to the LOCAL database, its 
integration tests pass, and its rollback SQL is recorded in the migration header and TRACK. Each gets a row in 
`spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/MIGRATIONS-PENDENTES.md`. Nothing is applied online before T15.
- **Online method (T15 only):** the Phase 4/5 method — re-check `npx supabase migration list --linked` and the target 
catalog immediately before; apply each reviewed file's SQL transactionally and record only its version; read back 
catalog objects; smoke-check. Never `supabase db push`, `migration up --linked`, or broad `migration repair`.
- **Supabase/RLS review gate (AGENTS.md):** every migration, RLS policy, grant, RPC, repository, and API route change 
passes the `supabase-rls-reviewer` audit (users.id vs supabase_uid, server client + `auth.getUser()`, service role 
never replacing authorization) before its task is recorded done.
- **Adversarial review gate (AGENTS.md):** direct Codex CLI, `gpt-6.1-sol`, effort `max`, read-only, per 
`delegation-anthropic.md`; prompts and results under `reviews/`. Per block, after its last task, over the block's 
combined diff: **Block A** = T1, T2, T3, T4; **Block B** = T5, T6, T7, T8; **Block C** = T9, T10, T11, T12, T13; 
**Final** = T14 over the whole work-item diff. Another round only for a High/Medium a real user or realistic failure 
can trigger; at most one fix round per block; leftovers recorded in TRACK and carried to T14.
- **Verification cadence (AGENTS.md, owner decisions 2026-10-10):** per task type-check + lint (new E2E specs are 
written with their task, not run); per block, after its fix round, type-check, lint, and the DB integration suite when 
server code changed; no E2E before T14; T14 runs every new spec and the full regression E2E once in Chrome only, zero 
retries, a failing test analysed and rerun alone. One test process at a time; nothing heavy in parallel.
- **Test policy (SPEC §15):** integration tests in a new `__tests__/meeting-notes-db/` suite (Vitest, node env, local 
Supabase, real routes — same pattern as `vitest.messaging-db.config.mts`) and Playwright E2E with two accounts. The 
external AI provider is the only thing replaced, by the local fake AI server built in T11. No unit tests; a touched 
unit test (e.g. `__tests__/company-settings-default-space.test.tsx`, `__tests__/space-detail-hover-panel.test.tsx`, 
`__tests__/modern-space-card.test.tsx`) is replaced by integration/E2E coverage and deleted, recorded in TRACK.
- **Secrets:** API keys and transcript text never in logs, errors, TRACK, reviews, or reports; tests use canary keys 
only.

## Observations grounding this plan (2026-10-13)

